 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Queueing Model Analysis for Food Delivery Logistics\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyzes food delivery systems using the **M/M/1 queueing model**. It focuses on performance metrics like waiting time, queue length, and system utilization.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Metrics:\n",
    "- **Utilization (ρ)**: The fraction of time the server is busy.\n",
    "- **Average Queue Length (Lq)**: Expected number of orders waiting in the queue.\n",
    "- **Average Waiting Time (Wq)**: Expected time an order waits in the queue.\n",
    "- **Average Time in System (W)**: Total time from order placement to delivery completion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set aesthetic style\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-muted')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = [10, 6]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Mathematical formulas for M/M/1 Queue\n",
    "\n",
    "Given:\n",
    "- Arrival Rate ($\lambda$)\n",
    "- Service Rate ($\mu$)\n",
    "\n",
    "Formulas:\n",
    "- $\rho = \lambda / \mu$\n",
    "- $L_q = \frac{\lambda^2}{\mu(\mu - \lambda)}$\n",
    "- $W_q = \frac{\lambda}{\mu(\mu - \lambda)}$\n",
    "- $W = \frac{1}{\mu - \lambda}$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def calculate_metrics(lam, mu):\n",
    "    if lam >= mu:\n",
    "        return None # System is unstable\n",
    "    rho = lam / mu\n",
    "    Lq = (lam**2) / (mu * (mu - lam))\n",
    "    Wq = lam / (mu * (mu - lam))\n",
    "    W = 1 / (mu - lam)\n",
    "    return rho, Lq, Wq, W\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulation Parameters\n",
    "arrival_rate = 0.8  # λ\n",
    "service_rate = 1.0  # μ\n",
    "\n",
    "metrics = calculate_metrics(arrival_rate, service_rate)\n",
    "if metrics:\n",
    "    rho, Lq, Wq, W = metrics\n",
    "    print(f\"Utilization (rho): {rho:.2f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Avg Queue Length (Lq): {Lq:.2f} orders\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Avg Waiting Time in Queue (Wq): {Wq:.2f} units\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Avg Total Time in System (W): {W:.2f} units\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Visualization: Waiting Time vs Arrival Rate\n",
    "\n",
    "Analyze how the system behaves as the arrival rate approaches the service capacity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mu = 1.0\n",
    "lambdas = np.linspace(0.1, 0.95, 50)\n",
    "waiting_times = [1 / (mu - l) for l in lambdas]\n",
    "queue_lengths = [(l**2) / (mu * (mu - l)) for l in lambdas]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax1 = plt.subplots()\n",
    "\n",
    "color = 'tab:blue'\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Arrival Rate (λ)')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Total Waiting Time (W)', color=color)\n",
    "ax1.plot(lambdas, waiting_times, color=color, linewidth=2, label='Waiting Time')\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor=color)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n",
    "color = 'tab:red'\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Queue Length (Lq)', color=color)\n",
    "ax2.plot(lambdas, queue_lengths, color=color, linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label='Queue Length')\n",
    "ax2.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor=color)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title('System Performance vs Arrival Rate (Service Rate μ = 1.0)')\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Real-Time Queue Simulation\n",
    "\n",
    "Simulating individual delivery orders over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "num_orders = 100\n",
    "inter_arrival_times = np.random.exponential(1/arrival_rate, num_orders)\n",
    "service_times = np.random.exponential(1/service_rate, num_orders)\n",
    "\n",
    "arrival_times = np.cumsum(inter_arrival_times)\n",
    "finish_times = np.zeros(num_orders)\n",
    "wait_times = np.zeros(num_orders)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(num_orders):\n",
    "    if i == 0:\n",
    "        finish_times[i] = arrival_times[i] + service_times[i]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        start_time = max(arrival_times[i], finish_times[i-1])\n",
    "        finish_times[i] = start_time + service_times[i]\n",
    "    wait_times[i] = finish_times[i] - arrival_times[i]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(range(num_orders), wait_times, marker='o', linestyle='-', color='purple', alpha=0.6)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Order Number')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Time in System')\n",
    "plt.title('Simulated Delivery Time per Order')\n",
    "plt.grid(True, which='both', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
